  "question": {
    "text": "Let $A=\\{z \\in C:|z-2-i|=3\\}$, $B=\\{z \\in C: \\operatorname{Re}(z-i z)=2\\}$ and $S=A \\cap B$. Then $\\sum_{z \\in S}|z|^2$ is equal to ________ .",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "22",
  "solution": {
    "text": "Let $z=x+i y$<br/>$\\begin{aligned}<br/>& A:|z-2-i|=3 \\\\\n& |(x-2)+(y-1) i|=3 \\\\\n& (x-2)^2+(y-1)^2=9 ....(1)\\\\\n& B=\\operatorname{Re}(z-i z)=2 \\\\\n& \\operatorname{Re}((x+y)+i(y-x))=2 \\\\\n& x+y=2....(2)<br/>\\end{aligned} .$<br/>On solving (1) and (2) we get<br/>$\\begin{aligned}<br/>& x=\\frac{3 \\pm \\sqrt{17}}{2}, y=\\frac{1 \\mp \\sqrt{17}}{2} \\\\\n& \\sum_{z \\in \\mathrm{~s}}|z|^2=\\frac{1}{4}[2 \\times 26+2 \\times 18] \\\\\n& \\Rightarrow \\frac{88}{4}=22<br/>\\end{aligned}$",
    "image": null
  },
